Step 4 : Building a Task Management Dashboard
Objective: Building the Responsive Dashboard

Core Prompt:
In the current application, create a responsive dashboard for a task management page. Include a sidebar navigation, main content area with task cards, statistics widgets, and a header with user menu. Use Tailwind CSS for styling with proper responsive breakpoints, dark mode support in the Navbar.tsx so it's accesible in the whole application, and accessibility features. To easily navigate between the pages, create a new /dashboard route, and include it in the current Navbar.tsx component.

Key Features:
    Sidebar Navigation: Collapsible on mobile, fixed on desktop
    Header: User menu dropdown, notifications
    Task Cards: Color-coded priorities, status indicators
    Statistics Widgets: Real-time metrics display

Dark Mode Toggle: Smooth theme transitions
    Dark Mode Implementation:
    Tailwind's dark: utility classes
    Theme switching with localStorage persistence
    Smooth color transitions
    Proper contrast ratios for accessibility

Responsive Breakpoints:
    Mobile (< 640px): Stacked layout, hamburger menu
    Tablet (640px - 1024px): Side-by-side with condensed sidebar
    Desktop (> 1024px): Full layout with expanded sidebar